<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Garsenda of Forcalquier</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Garsenda was countess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/forcalquier">Forcalquier</a>, the granddaughter and heiress of Count William IV. Her marriage in 1193 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-ii-count-of-provence">Alfonso II, Count of Provence</a>, brought Forcalquier back into union with Provence, and their son Ramon Berenguer IV ruled both. She is also counted among the trobairitz, the women troubadours of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/occitania">Occitania</a>, and was a patron of poets.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/garsenda-of-forcalquier.jpg" alt="Garsenda of Forcalquier" width="280" height="294" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis Blancard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gersenda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
